<p id="Sx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The authors declare that there is no conflict of interest in this paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendix</h2>

<div id="Sx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The appendix provides a detailed explanation of the derivation process for the allocation indices. Let <math id="Sx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of users. We represent the state of each user using a one-hot encoded vector of length 3, equal to the number of MEC servers. Specifically, the vector (1,0,0) indicates allocation to MEC server 1, (0,1,0) represents allocation to MEC server 2, and (0,0,1) denotes allocation to MEC server 3. Given a matrix <math id="Sx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="Sx3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> where each row represents the allocation state of a user in one-hot encoding, the objective is to convert this matrix into a single integer. Let <math id="Sx3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}=[x_{ia}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}=[x_{ia}]</annotation></semantics></math> be the given matrix where <math id="Sx3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> ranges from 0 to <math id="Sx3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> ranges from 0 to 2. Define a mapping function <math id="Sx3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\{(1,0,0),(0,1,0),(0,0,1)\}\to\{0,1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\{(1,0,0),(0,1,0),(0,0,1)\}\to\{0,1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The index <math id="Sx3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is then computed as</p>
<table id="Sx3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left"><math id="Sx3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}f(\mathbf{X}_{i})\cdot 3^{n-1-i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}f(\mathbf{X}_{i})\cdot 3^{n-1-i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_left_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Sx3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="Sx3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th row of matrix <math id="Sx3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
